# IYDT application verification

The eighteen child directories run deterministic checks of the IYDT application
forward models and analytical Jacobians. Each runner sources application code
from `../Code` and test cases from `../Test` relative to this directory.

## Suites and coverage

| Directory | Cases | Coverage |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `Seismic` | 14 | displacement/velocity models, alternate forms, and event derivatives |
| `Acoustic` | 14 | duration/impulse model variants and event derivatives |
| `Optical` | 5 | optical model variants and event derivatives |
| `Crater` | 6 | crater model variants and event derivatives |
| `Data` | 8 files | production data contracts and calibration/event model integration |
| `Transform` | deterministic | event transform round trips, Jacobians, log determinants, and boundaries |
| `Prior` | deterministic | event, calibration, yield, seismic, and optical prior gradients |
| `Checkpoint` | deterministic | calibration fit, pristine `.RData` copying, and event reuse |
| `Contract` | deterministic | rejection of missing covariates, short parameter vectors, and non-finite inputs |
| `Summary` | deterministic | structural output checks for calibration and event summaries |
| `Runfile` | reduced integration | actual `runMPEM.r` and `runMPEM_0.r` execution with a preserved calibration checkpoint |
| `Bayes` | bounded integration | fixed-seed Bayesian calibration/event sampling, likelihood/posterior gradients, EIV likelihood gradients, and pristine-checkpoint preservation |
| `Bayes-Backends` | bounded integration | real crater calibration/event sampling through both RAM and NUTS |
| `MultiPhenomenology` | bounded integration | optical and crater calibration outputs staged as `opt.RData` inputs to a combined calibration/event workflow |
| `Parallel` | bounded integration | deterministic crater calibration/event agreement with one and two workers |
| `Prediction` | reduced integration | direct forward-model agreement, observation identity, covariance inverse consistency, grouped residual dimensions, and determinism |
| `Profile` | reduced integration | five-point event profile likelihood, optimizer convergence, and generated plots |
| `Imputation` | bounded integration | two calibration-draw event analyses through RAM and SMC, pooled sample dimensions, diagnostics, and checkpoint preservation |

The case counts are the scripts sourced by each `tests.r`. Individual fixtures
use fixed random seeds and compare analytical derivatives with numerical
derivatives from `numDeriv`. The shared assertion helper checks dimensions and
finite values and fails the suite when the absolute/relative tolerance is
exceeded; printed differences are not treated as evidence of success.

## Recommended Docker workflow

No canonical symbolic links are needed. From `../../Test-Docker` run:

```text
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Seismic
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Acoustic
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Optical
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Crater
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Data
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Transform
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Prior
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Checkpoint
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Contract
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Summary
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Runfile
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Bayes
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Bayes-Backends
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/MultiPhenomenology
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Parallel
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Prediction
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Profile
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Imputation
```

Follow each printed job with `Rscript testmpem.R wait JOB`. The private snapshot
places IYDT code at `Test/IYDT/Code` and fixtures at `Test/IYDT/Test`, matching
the runners' relative paths.

## Native workflow

From `Test/IYDT`, create these links once:

```text
ln -s ../../Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp Code
ln -s ../../Applications/Test/IYDT Test
```

Install `numDeriv`, enter a suite directory, and run:

```text
R CMD BATCH tests.r tests.out &
```

The trailing `&` returns the shell prompt while the suite runs. Follow progress
with `tail -f tests.out` and wait for completion before assessing results.

The runner sources `forward.r`, `forward_0.r`, `jacobian.r`, and
`jacobian_0.r` before executing its cases. It writes `.RData` and `tests.out`
in the suite directory. Keep generated files out of the canonical tree when a
clean checkout is required; the Docker workflow does this automatically.

A successful test requires a zero process exit status. Preserve any pristine
benchmark or calibration `.RData` separately before using a workspace for an
event analysis; event-analysis output must not replace the calibration
checkpoint used for later events.

## Maintenance

When shared IYDT model, transform, prior, likelihood, posterior, prediction,
profile-likelihood, multiple-imputation, or summary code changes, run all
eighteen suites because
shared application files are sourced by every runner. Add a new fixture under
`../../Applications/Test/IYDT`, then source it explicitly from the appropriate
suite runner. A new suite directory containing `tests.r` is discovered by the
Docker launcher without changing the registry.
